text:
SALINAN
BUPATI DHARMASRAYA
PROVINSI SUMATERA BARAT
PERATURAN DAERAH KABUPATEN DHARMASRAYA
NOMOR 16 TAHUN 2018
TENTANG
PEMBERDAYAAN PEREMPUAN DAN PERLINDUNGANANAK
DENGAN RAHMAT TUHAN YANG MAHA ESA
BUPATI DHARMASRAYA,
Menimbang : a. bahwa perempuan dan anak berhak mendapatkanrasaaman dan bebas dari segala bentuk penyiksaanatau perlakuan yang merendahkan derajat martabat manusia; b. bahwa perempuan dan anak termasuk kelompok rentanyangcenderung mengalami kekerasan, sehinggaperlu mendapatkan perlindungan yang optimal;
c. bahwa pemenuhan hak-hak konstitusional perempuandan anak serta peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuandananak, merupakan salah satu urusan wajib yang menjadi tugas, wewenang dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah; d, bahwa berdasarkan pertimbangan sebagaimana dimaksuddalam huruf a, huruf b dan huruf c, perlumenetapkan Peraturan Daerah tentang Pemberdayaan PerempuandanPerlindungan Anak;
Mengingat : 1. Pasal 18 ayat (6) Undang-Undang Dasar NegaraRepublikIndonesia Tahun 1945;
2. Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2002 tentang PerlindunganAnak (Lembaran Negara Republik Indonesia Tahun2002Nomor 109, Tambahan Lembaran Negara RepublikIndonesia Nomor 4236) sebagaimana telah diubah beberapakali terakhir dengan Undang-Undang Nomor 17 Tahun2016tentang Penetapan Peraturan Pemerintah pengganti Undang- Undang Nomor 1 Tahun 2016 tentang Perubahankeduaatas Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2002 tentang PerlindunganAnak menjadi Undang-Undang (Lembaran NegaraRepublikIndonesia Tahun 2016 Nomor 237, TambahanLembaran Negara Republik Indonesia Nomor 5946);
3. Undang-Undang Nomor 38 Tahun 2003 tentang PembentukanKabupaten Dharmasraya, Kabupaten Solok SelatandanKabupaten Pasaman Barat di Provinsi SumateraBarat (Lembaran Negara Republik Indonesia Tahun 2003Nomor153, Tambahan Lembaran Negara Republik IndonesiaNomor
4348);
4. Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2004tentangPenghapusan Kekerasan Dalam Rumah Tangga (LembaranNegara Republik Indonesia Tahun 2004 Nomor 95,Tambahan Lembaran Negara Republik IndonesiaNomor
4419);
5. Undang-Undang Nomor 23 Tahun 2014tentangPemerintahan Daerah (Lembaran Negara RepublikIndonesia Tahun 2014), sebagaimana telah diubah beberapakali,terakhir dengan Undang-Undang Nomor 32 Tahun2004tentang Perubahan Ketiga Atas Undang-Undang Nomor23 Tahun 2014 tentang Pemerintahan Daerah (LembaranNegaraRepublik Indonesia Tahun 2014);
6. Peraturan Daerah Provinsi Sumatera Barat Nomor 5Tahun2013 tentang Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak(LembaranDaerah Provinsi Sumatera Barat Tahun 2013 Nomor5,Tambahan Lembaran Daerah Provinsi Sumatera Barat Nomor88);
Dengan Persetujuan Bersama DEWAN PERWAKILAN RAKYAT DAERAH KABUPATEN DHARMASRAYAdan

translated_text:
COPY
REGENT OF DHARMASRAYA
WEST SUMATRA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF DHARMASRAYA REGENCY
NUMBER 16 OF 2018
CONCERNING
WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF DHARMASRAYA,
Considering : a. that women and children have the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of torture or treatment that degrades human dignity; b. that women and children are vulnerable groups who tend to experience violence, therefore they need to obtain optimal protection;
c. that the fulfillment of constitutional rights of women and children as well as the improvement of the quality of life of women and children, is one of the mandatory affairs that becomes the duty, authority and responsibility of the Regional Government; d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4236) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);
3. Law Number 38 of 2003 concerning the Establishment of Dharmasraya Regency, South Solok Regency and West Pasaman Regency in West Sumatra Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
4348);
4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
4419);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014), as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning the Third Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014);
6. Regional Regulation of West Sumatra Province Number 5 of 2013 concerning the Protection of Women and Children (Regional Gazette of West Sumatra Province of 2013 Number 5, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of West Sumatra Province Number 88);
With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF DHARMASRAYA REGENCY and

text:
Pasal 2
(1) Penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan berdasarkanasas :
a. kepentingan terbaik bagi perempuan;
b. keadilan gender dan kesetaraan gender; c. kearifan lokal; dan
d. kepastian hukum.
(2) Penyelenggaraan perlindungan anak berdasarkanasas: a. non diskriminasi;
b. kepentingan yang terbaik bagi anak;
c. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup, danperkembangan;
d. penghargaan terhadap pendapat anak; dan e. kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2
(1) The implementation of protection for women is based on the principles of:
 a. the best interests of women;
 b. gender justice and gender equality;
 c. local wisdom; and
 d. legal certainty.
(2) The implementation of protection for children is based on the principles of:
 a. non-discrimination;
 b. the best interests of the child;
 c. the right to life, survival, and development;
 d. respect for the views of the child; and
 e. legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 3
Pemberdayaan perempuan dan Perlindungan anak bertujuan: a. sebagai pedoman bagi pemerintah daerahdalamperencanaan, kebijakan dan strategi perlindunganperempuan dan anak;
b. melindungi perempuan dan anak dari tindakan, keputusandan kebijakan yang melanggar hak perempuan dananak; c. mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran hak perempuandananak;
d. meningkatkan pemberdayaan terhadap perempuandananak;
e. meningkatkan peran dan nilai kearifan lokal sertaperananadat dalam perlindungan perempuan dan anak; danf. meningkatkan peran lembaga pemerintahdannonpemerintah di daerah dalam upaya perlindunganperempuandan anak.

translated_text:
Article 3
Women's Empowerment and Child Protection aims to:
a. serve as a guideline for local government in planning, policies and strategies for the protection of women and children;
b. protect women and children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and children;
c. prevent violations of the rights of women and children;
d. increase empowerment of women and children;
e. enhance the role and value of local wisdom and the role of customs in the protection of women and children; and
f. enhance the role of government and non-government institutions in the region in efforts to protect women and children.

text:
Pasal 4
Ruang lingkup pengaturan perlindungan perempuandananakmeliputi:
a. hak dan kewajiban;
b. peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan;
c. perlindungan perempuan dan anak; d. peningkatan kualitas keluarga;
e. sistem data gender dan anak;
f. pemenuhan hak anak;
g. kabupaten layak anak; dan
h. pembinaan dan pengawasan.

translated_text:
Article 4
The scope of regulation for the protection of women and children includes:
a. rights and obligations;
b. improvement of women's quality of life;
c. protection of women and children;
d. improvement of family quality;
e. gender and child data system;
f. fulfillment of children's rights;
g. child-friendly regency; and
h. guidance and supervision.

text:
Pasal 5
Setiap perempuan berhak:
a. memperoleh perlindungan dari tindakan diskriminasi; b. memperoleh perlindungan dari eksploitasi ekonomi daneksploitasi seksual;
c. memperoleh perlindungan dari kekerasan fisik, psikologis,seksual, dan penelantaran;
d. memperoleh pekerjaan yang layak sesuai kemampuannya; e. memperoleh cuti kerja dengan menerima upah/gaji sesuai peraturan perundang-undangan;
f. memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran di semuajenis,jenjang dan jalur pendidikan;
g. mendapatkan perlindungan khusus dalampelaksanaanpekerjaan atau profesinya terhadap hal-hal yangdapatmengancam keselamatan dan atau kesehatannya berkenaandengan fungsi reproduksi perempuan; dan
h. pemilikan dan pengelolaan harta bersamadalamperkawinan sesuai dengan peraturan perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
Article 5
Every woman has the right to:
a. obtain protection from discriminatory actions;
b. obtain protection from economic exploitation and sexual exploitation;
c. obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;
d. obtain decent work in accordance with her capabilities;
e. obtain work leave while receiving wages/salary in accordance with statutory regulations;
f. obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education;
g. obtain special protection in the implementation of her work or profession against matters that could threaten her safety and or health in relation to women's reproductive function; and
h. ownership and management of joint property in marriage in accordance with statutory regulations.

text:
Pasal 6
Setiap anak berhak :
a. untuk hidup, tumbuh, berkembang dan berpartisipasi secara wajar sesuai harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan; b. memperoleh perlindungan dari tindakan diskriminasi; c. memperoleh perlindungan dari eksploitasi ekonomi daneksploitasi seksual;
d. memperoleh perlindungan dari kekerasan fisik, psikologis,seksual, dan penelantaran;
e. atas suatu nama sebagai identitas diri danstatuskewarganegaraan;
f. memperoleh akta kelahiran secara bebas biaya ; g. untuk memeluk agama dan beribadah menurut ajaranagamanya dengan bimbingan orang tua/wali; h. untuk tidak dipaksa berganti agama oleh orang tuaasuh,orang tua angkat dan oleh siapapun;
i. untuk diakui dan mengetahui orang tuanya, dibesarkandandiasuh oleh orang tuanya sendiri;
j. memperoleh pelayanan kesehatan dan jaminansosial sesuai dengan kebutuhan fisik, mental, spiritual, dan sosial. k. memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran sesuai denganminat dan bakatnya;
l. memperoleh perawatan, pendidikan, pelatihan,meningkatkan diri dan kemampuan berpartisipasi dalamkehidupan bermasyarakat dan bernegara bagi anakpenyandang disabilitas fisik, mental dan berkebutuhankhusus;
m. menyampaikan dan didengar pendapatnya; dann. beristirahat dan memanfaatkan waktu luangdemi pengembangan diri.

translated_text:
Article 6
Every child has the right:
a. to live, grow, develop and participate reasonably in accordance with human dignity;
b. to obtain protection from acts of discrimination;
c. to obtain protection from economic exploitation and sexual exploitation;
d. to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;
e. to a name as personal identity and citizenship status;
f. to obtain a birth certificate free of charge;
g. to embrace a religion and worship according to the teachings of their religion with the guidance of parents/guardians;
h. not to be forced to change religion by foster parents, adoptive parents, or anyone;
i. to be recognized and to know their parents, and to be raised and cared for by their own parents;
j. to obtain health services and social security in accordance with physical, mental, spiritual, and social needs;
k. to obtain education and teaching in accordance with their interests and talents;
l. to obtain care, education, training, self-improvement and the ability to participate in community and state life for children with physical and mental disabilities and special needs;
m. to express and have their opinion heard; and
n. to rest and utilize leisure time for self-development.

Article 7
The obligations of the Regional Government in efforts to protect women include:
a. establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women's rights;
b. conducting cooperation with the community and/or Community Organizations in the implementation of women's protection in accordance with laws and regulations;
c. conducting rehabilitation and empowerment of women who are victims of acts of violence;
d. providing special protection to women victims of acts of violence and human trafficking; and
e. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations of women's rights.

text:
Pasal 8
Kewajiban Pemerintah Daerah dalamupaya perlindunganterhadap anak meliputi:
a. menjamin hak asasi setiap anak tanpa diskriminasi; b. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasaranadalampenyelenggaraan perlindungan anak;
c. menjamin hak anak untuk menyampaikanpendapatsesuai dengan usia dan tingkat kecerdasan anak; d. menetapkan dan melaksanakan kebijakansertaprogram/kegiatan perlindungan terhadap hak anak; e. melakukan kerjasama dengan masyarakat dan/atauOrganisasi Kemasyarakatan dalampenyelenggaraanperlindungan anak sesuai peraturan perundang-undangan; f. melakukan rehabilitasi terhadap anak yang menjadi korbantindak kekerasan;
g. memberikan perlindungan khusus kepada anakdalamsituasi darurat, anak yang berhadapan denganhukum, anak korban tindak kekerasan dan perdaganganorang, anak dari kelompok minoritas dan terisolasi, anaktereksploitasi secara ekonomi dan/atau seksual, anakyang menjadi korban penyalahgunaan narkotika, alkohol, psikotropika dan anak dengan HIV/AIDS;
h. menyelenggarakan pendidikan inklusif bagi anakyangberkebutuhan khusus; dan
i. melakukan tindakan preventif dalamrangka mencegahterjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak anak.

translated_text:
Article 8
The obligations of the Regional Government in efforts to protect children include:
a. guaranteeing the human rights of every child without discrimination; b. providing support for facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of child protection;
c. guaranteeing the right of children to express their opinions in accordance with the age and intelligence level of the child; d. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the protection of children's rights; e. cooperating with the community and/or Community Organizations in the implementation of child protection in accordance with laws and regulations; f. conducting rehabilitation for children who are victims of acts of violence;
g. providing special protection to children in emergency situations, children in conflict with the law, children who are victims of acts of violence and human trafficking, children from minority and isolated groups, children who are economically and/or sexually exploited, children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic substance abuse and children with HIV/AIDS;
h. organizing inclusive education for children with special needs; and
i. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations of children's rights.

Article 11
(1) Parents, in efforts to protect the rights of children, are obligated to:
   a. care for, maintain, educate, and protect children;
   b. develop children in accordance with their abilities, talents, and interests;
   c. provide formal and non-formal education;
   d. guide children to behave in accordance with religion, ethics and morals as well as customs; and
   e. prevent the occurrence of marriage at a child's age.
(2) In the event that parents do not exist, or their whereabouts are unknown, or due to a reason cannot carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may transfer to the family.

text:
Pasal 12
(1) Dalam rangka meningkatkan kualitas hidup perempuan,Pemerintah Daerah bertanggungjawab:
a. menghormati dan menjamin hak perempuantanpadiskriminasi sesuai dengan harkat danmartabatkemanusian;
b. melaksanakan Pengarustamaan Gender di Daerah; c. membentuk pokja Pengarustamaan Gender di Daerah; d. meningkatkan pemberdayaan Perempuan dalamperan,kualitas dan kemampuan di bidang:
1. politik;
2. hukum;
3. sosial; dan
4. ekonomi.
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedialayanan pemberdayaan perempuan di daerah. (2) Tanggungjawab pemerintah daerah dalamupaya peningkatankualitas hidup perempuan sebagaimana dimaksudpadaayat(1) dilaksanakan oleh Perangkat Daerah terkait.

translated_text:
Article 12
(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:
a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity and worth;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Region;
c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region;
d. increasing the empowerment of Women in terms of role, quality and capacity in the fields of:
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social; and
4. economy.
e. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for women's empowerment in the region.
(2) The responsibility of the regional government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by the relevant Regional Apparatus.

text:
Pasal 16
Pokja Pengarustamaan Gender Daerah sebagaimana dimaksuddalam Pasal 15 ayat (1) mempunyai tugas sebagai berikut: a. mempromosikan dan memfasilitasi PengarustamaanGenderkepada masing-masing Perangkat Daerah;
b. melaksanakan sosialisasi dan advokasi PengarustamaanGender kepada Camat dan Wali Nagari;
c. menyusun program kerja setiap tahun; d. mendorong terwujudnya perencanaan dan penganggaranyangresponsif gender;
e. menyusun rencana kerja pokja PengarustamaanGendersetiap tahun;
f. bertanggungjawab kepada Bupati melalui Wakil Bupati; g. merumuskan rekomendasi kebijakan PengarustamaanGender kepada Bupati;
h. menyusun profil Gender Daerah;
i. melakukan pemantauan pelaksanaan PengarustamaanGender dimasing-masing Perangkat Daerah.
j. menetapkan tim teknis untuk melakukan analisis terhadapanggaran daerah responsif gender;
k. menyusun rencana aksi daerah tentang PengarustamaanGender di daerah; dan
l. mendorong dilaksanakannya pemilihan dan penetapanfocal point di masing-masing Perangkat Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 16
The Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 15 paragraph (1) has the following duties:
a. promoting and facilitating Gender Mainstreaming to each Regional Apparatus;
b. implementing socialization and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to Sub-district Heads and Wali Nagari;
c. preparing work programs every year;
d. encouraging the realization of gender-responsive planning and budgeting;
e. preparing the work plan of the Gender Mainstreaming working group every year;
f. being responsible to the Regent through the Vice Regent;
g. formulating Gender Mainstreaming policy recommendations to the Regent;
h. preparing the Regional Gender profile;
i. conducting monitoring of Gender Mainstreaming implementation in each Regional Apparatus;
j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the gender-responsive regional budget;
k. preparing a regional action plan on Gender Mainstreaming in the region; and
l. encouraging the implementation of selection and determination of focal points in each Regional Apparatus.

text:
Pasal 17
(1) Tim teknis sebagaimana dimaksud dalamPasal 16huruf j beranggotakan aparatur yang memahami analisis anggaranresponsif gender.
(2) Rencana aksi daerah Pengarustamaan Gender Daerahsebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 16 huruf k memuat : a. pengarustamaan gender dalam peraturan perundang-undangan di daerah;
b. pengarustamaan gender dalam siklus pembangunandi daerah;
c. penguatan kelembagaan Pengarustamaan Genderdi daerah; dan
d. penguatan peran serta masyarakat di daerah

translated_text:
Article 17
(1) The technical team as referred to in Article 16 letter j shall consist of apparatus who understand gender responsive budget analysis.
(2) The regional action plan for Regional Gender Mainstreaming as referred to in Article 16 letter k shall contain: a. gender mainstreaming in laws and regulations in the region;
b. gender mainstreaming in the development cycle in the region;
c. institutional strengthening of Gender Mainstreaming in the region; and
d. strengthening of community participation in the region

text:
Pasal 18
(1) Focal Point Pengarusutamaan Gender pada setiapPerangkatDaerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalamPasal 16 huruf l terdiri dari pejabat dan/atau staf yang membidangi tugasperencanaan dan/atau program (2) Focal Point Pengarusutamaan Gender sebagaimana dimaksudpada ayat (1), mempunyai tugas:
a. mempromosikan Pengarusutamaan Gender padaunitkerja;
b. memfasilitasi penyusunan rencana kerjadanpenganggaran Perangkat Daerah yang responsif gender; c. melaksanakan pelatihan, sosialisasi, advokasi Pengarusutamaan Gender kepada seluruh pejabat danstaf di lingkungan Perangkat Daerah;
d. melaporkan pelaksanaan PengarusutamaanGenderkepada pimpinan Perangkat Daerah;
e. mendorong pelaksanaan analisis gender terhadapkebijakan, program, dan kegiatan pada unit kerja; danf. memfasilitasi penyusunan data gender padamasing-masing Perangkat Daerah.
(3) Focal Point Pengarusutamaan Gender sebagaimana dimaksudpada ayat (1), dipilih dan ditetapkan oleh pimpinanPerangkatDaerah

translated_text:
Article 18
(1) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point in each Regional Apparatus as referred to in Article 16 letter l consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or programs.
(2) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1) has the following duties:
  a. promoting Gender Mainstreaming in work units;
  b. facilitating the preparation of work plans and budgeting of Regional Apparatus that are gender responsive;
  c. conducting training, socialization, and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the Regional Apparatus;
  d. reporting the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming to the leadership of the Regional Apparatus;
  e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis on policies, programs, and activities in work units; and
  f. facilitating the preparation of gender data in each Regional Apparatus.
(3) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be selected and determined by the leadership of the Regional Apparatus.

text:
Pasal 19
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuanperempuan dalam bidang politik meliputi:
a. melaksanakan sosialisasi untuk meningkatkanpartisipasi politik perempuan dalam pemilihan umum; b. melaksanakan program yang mendorong tingkatketerlibatan perempuan dalam proses politik danjabatanpublik;
c. melakukan fasilitasi pengembangan diri perempuandalamberorganisasi, berserikat dan berkumpul;
d. melibatkan perempuan dalam pengambilan keputusanyangmenyangkut kepentingan perempuan;

translated_text:
Article 19
Efforts to increase the role, quality, and capability of women in the political field include:
a. conducting outreach to increase women's political participation in general elections;
b. implementing programs that encourage the level of women's involvement in the political process and public positions;
c. facilitating women's self-development in organizing, associating, and gathering;
d. involving women in decision-making concerning women's interests;

text:
Pasal 21
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuanperempuandalam bidang sosial meliputi:
a. peningkatan pengetahuan dan keterampilanuntukmendorong pemenuhan pendidikan sesuai denganpotensi yang dimiliki;
b. peningkatan dan pemenuhan kualitas kesehatanterhadapperempuan;
c. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuantentangperencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahteratermasukakses layanan konsultasi dan pencatatan perkawinan;
d. peningkatan kesadaran perempuan terhadapdampakpernikahan dini;
e. memfasilitasi dan mengupayakan pelestarian adat istiadat danpengembangan ilmu pengetahuan, teknologi, seni danbudayauntuk kemajuan perempuan;
f. melakukan peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuanperempuan terhadap perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehatdan sejahtera;
g. melakukan program dalam menurunkan angka kematianibumelahirkan;
h. mendorong pembentukan organisasi perempuan di Daerah;

translated_text:
Article 21
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the social field include:
a. increasing knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in accordance with the potential possessed;
b. increasing and fulfilling the quality of health for women;
c. increasing awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. increasing women's awareness of the impact of early marriage;
e. facilitating and endeavoring to preserve customs and traditions and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. increasing women's awareness and knowledge of independent, healthy and prosperous family planning;
g. implementing programs to reduce maternal mortality rates;
h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the Region;

text:
Pasal 22
Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuanperempuandalam bidang meliputi:
a. melaksanakan program, kegiatan, pelatihanuntukpeningkatan keterampilan dan keahlian perempuandalamrangka mewujudkan peningkatan kesejahteraan perempuan;
b. fasilitasi penguatan modal usaha bagi perempuanyangmemiliki ekonomi lemah;
c. pemasaran produk hasil usaha perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi lemah;
d. pelatihan pengembangan kemampuan perempuanmelalui pemberdayaan ekonomi keluarga prasejahtera; e. pelatihan kewirausahaan kepada perempuansecarakomprehensif.

translated_text:
Article 22
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the field include:
a. implementing programs, activities, and training to improve women's skills and expertise in order to realize an improvement in women's welfare;
b. facilitating the strengthening of business capital for women with weak economic conditions;
c. marketing products resulting from the businesses of women with weak economic conditions;
d. training to develop women's capabilities through the economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families;
e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

text:
Pasal 23
(1) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah untuk mencegahterjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuandananakmeliputi:
a. menyelenggarakan sosialisasi mengenai pencegahankekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anakdenganmengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat, budaya, agamadanorganisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. menyediakan pedoman tentang penanganantindakkekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak; c. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalampemulihandanreintegrasi;
d. mengembangkan database dan sisteminformasi yangterintegrasi tentang tindak kekerasanterhadapperempuan dan anak;
e. mengembangkan program pemberdayaan keluarga;
f. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatanyangbergerak dibidang pemberdayaan perempuandanperlindungan anak; dan
g. menyediakan fasilitas umum yang nyamandanamanuntuk perempuan dan anak.
(2) Pencegahan terjadinya tindak kekerasan perempuandananak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), dilaksanakanolehPerangkat Daerah yang tugas dan fungsinya di bidang: a. sosial;
b. kesehatan;
c. pendidikan;
d. ketenagakerjaan;
e. pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungananak; f. mental dan spiritual;
g. informatika dan komunikasi; dan h. ketentraman dan ketertiban.
(3) Pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),dilaksanakan oleh Perangkat Daerah sesuai denganbidangtugasnya secara terpadu dan berkesinambunganberdasarkanRencana Aksi Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 23
(1) The responsibility of the Regional Government to prevent acts of violence against women and children includes:
a. conducting socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. providing guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children;
c. involving community participation in recovery and reintegration;
d. developing an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against women and children;
e. developing family empowerment programs;
f. strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. providing public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and
h. public peace and order.
(3) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

text:
Pasal 24
Tangungjawab masyarakat untuk mencegah terjadinyatindakkekerasan terhadap perempuan dan Anak meliputi: a. mengawasi berbagai kondisi yang terjadi di lingkungannya yang dapat menimbulkan pelanggaran terhadaphakperempuan dan anak;
b. meningkatkan kepedulian terhadap pelanggaranhakperempuan dan anak;
c. menguatkan peran organisasi kemasyarakatan, keagamaandan lingkungan keluarga; dan
d. mencegah pernikahan di bawah tangan dan perkawinanpadausia anak.

translated_text:
Article 24
The responsibility of the community to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children includes:
a. monitoring various conditions that occur in their environment that may give rise to violations of the rights of women and children;
b. increasing awareness of violations of the rights of women and children;
c. strengthening the role of community organizations, religious organizations and the family environment; and
d. preventing unregistered marriages and marriage at the age of a child.

text:
Pasal 25
Tanggungjawab orang tua dan keluarga untuk mencegahterjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuandananakmeliputi:
a. melindungi perempuan dan anak dari berbagai pelanggaranhak dalam rumah tangga;
b. mendorong terbentuknya keluarga yang harmonis, edukatifdan demokratis;
c. memberikan tauladan yang baik kepada anak sesuai ajaranagama dan adat;
d. mengawasi anak dalam beraktifitas di dalamataupundi luarrumah; dan
e. memberikan peluang bagi anak berdialog menyampaikanpendapat secara demokratis.

translated_text:
Article 25
The responsibility of parents and family to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children includes:
a. protecting women and children from various violations of rights in the household;
b. encouraging the formation of a harmonious, educational and democratic family;
c. providing good examples to children in accordance with religious and customary teachings;
d. supervising children in their activities inside or outside the home; and
e. providing opportunities for children to dialogue and express opinions democratically.

text:
Pasal 26
(1) Dalam rangka melaksanakan Perlindungan PerempuandanAnak di Daerah, Pemerintah Daerah membentukUPTDPPAsesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.
(2) UPTD PPA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berfungsi untuk memberikan layanan terhadap perempuandanAnakyang mengalami permasalahan pidana dan/atauperdata.
(3) Lingkup pelayanan UPTD PPA sebagaimana dimaksudpadaayat (2) meliputi:
a. pelayanan pengaduan;
b. rehabilitasi kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. pendampingan;
e. penegakan dan bantuan hukum; dan f. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
(4) Dalam melaksanakan fungsinya UPTD PPA berkewajiban: a. memberikan pelayanan dan penanganan secepat mungkinkepada perempuan dan anak yang mengalami permasalahan;
b. memberikan kemudahan, kenyamanan, keselamatandanbebas biaya kepada perempuan dan anak yang mengalami permasalahan;
c. menjaga kerahasiaan perempuan dan anakyangmengalami permasalahan;
d. menjamin keadilan dan kepastian hukumbagi perempuandan anak yang mengalami permasalahan.
(5) UPTD PPA bertanggung jawab kepada Perangkat Daerahyangmenyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan di bidangPemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 26
(1) In order to implement the Protection of Women and Children in the Region, the Regional Government establishes UPTD PPA in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) functions to provide services to women and Children who experience criminal and/or civil problems.
(3) The scope of services of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
 a. complaint services;
 b. health rehabilitation;
 c. social rehabilitation;
 d. assistance;
 e. enforcement and legal aid; and
 f. repatriation and social reintegration.
(4) In carrying out its functions, UPTD PPA is obligated to:
 a. provide services and handling as quickly as possible to women and children who experience problems;
 b. provide convenience, comfort, safety and free of charge to women and children who experience problems;
 c. maintain the confidentiality of women and children who experience problems;
 d. guarantee justice and legal certainty for women and children who experience problems.
(5) UPTD PPA is responsible to the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

text:
Pasal 29
Pelayanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalamPasal 26ayat (3) huruf a dapat dikoordinasikan oleh UPTDPPAdenganinstansi terkait yang terdiri dari:
a. rumah sakit;
b. pusat kesehatan masyarakat;
c. pusat pelayanan terpadu pemberdayaan perempuandananakd. rumah perlindungan trauma center;
d. women crisis centre;
e. badan penasehat pembinaan dan pelestarian perkawinan; f. kepolisian;
g. kejaksaan;
h. pengadilan;
i. kementerian agama; dan/atau j. organisasi bantuan hukum;

translated_text:
Article 29
Complaint services as referred to in Article 26 paragraph (3) letter a may be coordinated by UPTD PPA with related agencies consisting of:
a. hospitals;
b. public health centers;
c. integrated service centers for women and children empowerment;
d. trauma center protection houses/shelters;
e. women crisis centres;
f. advisory board for marriage guidance and preservation;
g. police;
h. prosecutor's office;
i. courts;
j. ministry of religious affairs; and/or legal aid organizations;

text:
Pasal 31
(1) Rehabilitasi kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalamPasal 26ayat (3) huruf b merupakan upaya yang meliputi aspek: a. promotif, meningkatkan agar status kesehatansemakinmeningkat;
b. preventif, mencegah jangan sampai terkena penyakit; c. kuratif, menyembuhkan seseorang dari sakit secarafisikdan psikis;
d. rehabilitatif, menjaga agar seseorang yangbelumsepenuhnya sembuh agar bisa kembali bugar seperti semula.
(2) Rehabilitasi kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud padaayat (1) dilakukan secara komprehensif, dapat diakses 24 (duapuluhempat) jam, berkualitas dan dilakukan sesuai denganstandarpelayanan kesehatan.
(3) Perempuan dan Anak korban tindak kekerasan memiliki hakterhadap pelayanan kesehatan dengan bebas biaya, meliputi: a. pelayanan medis;
b. pelayanan medikolegal;
c. konseling psikososial; dan
d. Visum er Repertum.
(4) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai tata cara pelaksanaanpelayanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud padaayat (3) diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 31
(1) Health rehabilitation as referred to in Article 26 paragraph (3) letter b constitutes efforts that include the following aspects:
a. promotive, improving so that health status increasingly improves;
b. preventive, preventing so as not to become ill;
c. curative, curing a person from illness physically and psychologically;
d. rehabilitative, maintaining so that a person who has not fully recovered can return to being fit as before.
(2) Health rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted comprehensively, accessible 24 (twenty-four) hours, with quality and conducted in accordance with health service standards.
(3) Women and Children victims of acts of violence have the right to health services free of charge, including:
a. medical services;
b. medicolegal services;
c. psychosocial counseling; and
d. Visum et Repertum.
(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for implementing health services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 33
(1) Pelayanan konseling sebagaimana dimaksud dalamPasal 32ayat (2) huruf a bertujuan:
a. membantu perempuan dan Anak korbantindakkekerasan mengenali permasalahannya dan menemukancara yang efektif untuk mengatasinya sendiri;
b. memberdayakan perempuan dan anak yang mengalami permasalahan pidana dan/atau perdatauntukmenentukan masa depannya;
c. memberikan dukungan moral terhadap perempuandananak yang mengalami permasalahan pidana dan/atauperdata dalam menghadapi proses yang dijalaninya; dan
d. membuat perempuan dan anak yang mengalami permasalahan pidana dan/atau perdata merasaditerimadi lingkungan masyarakat.
(2) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial yang responsif gender, terdiri atas:
a. konselor;
b. psikolog; dan/atau
c. psikiater.
(3) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan di tempat yang menjaminrasaaman, nyaman dan kerahasiaan informasi dari perempuankorban tindak kekerasan.
(4) Tahapan pelayanan konseling sebagaimana dimaksudpadaayat (3) meliputi:
a. konseling awal;
b. konseling lanjutan;
c. pembahasan kasus; dan
d. kunjungan ke lokasi.

translated_text:
Article 33
(1) Counseling services as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (2) letter a aim to:
a. assist women and children victims of acts of violence in recognizing their problems and finding effective ways to overcome them independently;
b. empower women and children experiencing criminal and/or civil problems to determine their future;
c. provide moral support to women and children experiencing criminal and/or civil problems in facing the process they are undergoing; and
d. make women and children experiencing criminal and/or civil problems feel accepted in the community environment.
(2) Counseling services are carried out by gender-responsive social rehabilitation officers, consisting of:
a. counselors;
b. psychologists; and/or
c. psychiatrists.
(3) Counseling services are carried out in a place that guarantees a sense of security, comfort and confidentiality of information from women victims of acts of violence.
(4) The stages of counseling services as referred to in paragraph (4) include:
a. initial counseling;
b. follow-up counseling;
c. case discussion; and
d. site visits.

text:
Pasal 43
Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud dalamPasal 42huruf a,meliputi:
a. tumbuh kembang Anak balita;
b. perlindungan terhadap kesehatan reproduksi remaja; c. pendewasaan usia perkawinan;
d. pengaturan kelahiran; dan
e. meningkatkan kualitas kesehatan ibu hamil dan menyusui.

translated_text:
Article 43
Guidance as referred to in Article 42 letter a, includes:
a. growth and development of children under five years old;
b. protection of adolescent reproductive health;
c. maturation of marriage age;
d. birth regulation; and
e. improving the health quality of pregnant and breastfeeding mothers.

text:
Pasal 44
Bimbingan sebagaimana dimaksud Pasal 42 huruf b meliputi: a. melakukan penyuluhan peningkatan kualitas hidupperempuan;
b. melakukan penyuluhan pranikah; dan c. fasilitasi penyelenggaraan pembangunan keluarga;

translated_text:
Article 44
Guidance as referred to in Article 42 letter b includes:
a. conducting counseling on improving the quality of women's lives;
b. conducting premarital counseling; and
c. facilitating the implementation of family development;

Article 46
The provision of services for families as referred to in Article 41 paragraph (1) letter b includes:
a. communication, information and education;
b. recording and reporting of family planning services;
c. adequate facilities and infrastructure for health services; and
d. lactation rooms in every public facility.

text:
Pasal 48
(1) Instansi dan pihak swasta yang menyelenggarakanpelayananpublik wajib menyediakan ruangan laktasi. (2) Ruangan laktasi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan ruangan yang layak dan memadai. (3) Pimpinan Instansi yang tidak menyediakan ruanganlaktasi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dikenakansanksi administratif berupa :
a. teguran tertulis; dan/atau
b. sanksi kepegawaian berdasarkan ketentuanPeraturanPerundang-Undangan.
(4) Pihak swasta yang tidak menyediakan ruanganlaktasi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dikenai sanksi administratif berupa:
a. peringatan tertulis;
b. pembatasan kegiatan usaha;
c. pembekuan kegiatan usaha;
d. denda administratif; dan/atau e. pencabutan izin.

Pasal 51
Pokja data terpilah gender dan anak sebagaimana dimaksuddalam Pasal 50 mempunyai tugas :
a. menyusun rencana kerja kelompok kerja data terpilahgenderdan anak dengan menggunakan indikator dan target terukuruntuk periode tertentu yang akan digunakanuntukmonitoring dan evaluasi kegiatan kelompok kerja dataterpilahgender dan anak;
b. meningkatkan kerjasama lintas sektor dalamrangkapenguatan data yang dihasilkan terkait denganpengadaandan pemanfaatan data;
c. melaksanakan koordinasi dan sinkronisasi denganinstansi terkait dalam rangka penyusunan data gender dananakuntuk tingkat Daerah; dan
d. menghimpun, mengolah, menyusun dan meningkatkankualitas data serta mempresentasikan data di organisasi perangkat daerah dan selanjutnya dijadikan data sekunderpada data Gender dan Anak secara berkesinambungan.

translated_text:
Article 51
The gender and child disaggregated data working group as referred to in Article 50 has the following duties:
a. prepare a work plan for the gender and child disaggregated data working group using indicators and measurable targets for a specific period to be used for monitoring and evaluation of the gender and child disaggregated data working group activities;
b. enhance cross-sectoral cooperation in the framework of strengthening data produced related to the procurement and utilization of data;
c. implement coordination and synchronization with relevant agencies in the framework of compiling gender and child data for the Regional level; and
d. collect, process, compile and improve the quality of data as well as present data in regional apparatus organizations and subsequently make it secondary data for Gender and Child data on an ongoing basis.

text:
Pasal 52
(1) Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya pemenuhanhakAnakbertanggungjawab:
a. menetapkan dan melaksanakan kebijakansertaprogram/kegiatan pemenuhan hak Anak;
b. menghormati dan menjamin hak asasi setiap Anakdengantidak membedakan suku, agama, ras, golongan, jeniskelamin, etnik, budaya dan bahasa, status hukumAnak,urutan kelahiran Anak, dan kondisi fisik dan/ataumental;
c. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedialayanan peningkatan kualitas keluarga dalammewujudkanhak Anak;
d. menjamin Perlindungan, pemeliharaan, dan kesejahteraanAnak dengan memperhatikan hak dan kewajibanorangtua,wali, atau orang lain yang secara hukumbertanggungjawabterhadap Anak;
e. menyediakan sarana dan prasarana dalampenyelenggaraan pemenuhan hak Anak;
f. menjamin hak Anak untuk menyampaikan pendapat sesuai dengan usia dan tingkat kecerdasan Anak; g. melakukan pengawasan dan pembinaan dalamrangkapenyelenggaraan pemenuhan hak Anak; dan h. melakukan kerjasama dengan pihak swasta dan/atauLSMdalam penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Anak; (2) Tanggungjawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh Perangkat Daerah sesuai dengantugasdanfungsinya.

translated_text:
Article 52
(1) Regional Government in the effort to fulfill the rights of Children is responsible for:
a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the fulfillment of Children's rights;
b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every Child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnic group, culture and language, legal status of the Child, birth order of the Child, and physical and/or mental condition;
c. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for improving family quality in realizing Children's rights;
d. guaranteeing the Protection, care, and welfare of Children by taking into account the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, or other persons who are legally responsible for the Child;
e. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of the fulfillment of Children's rights;
f. guaranteeing the right of Children to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the Child;
g. conducting supervision and guidance in the framework of implementing the fulfillment of Children's rights; and
h. conducting cooperation with private parties and/or NGOs in the implementation of Child Protection;
(2) The responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
Pasal 59
(1) Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyelenggarakanlayanankesehatan yang komprehensif bagi Anak, agar setiapAnakmemperoleh derajat kesehatan yang optimal sejakdalamkandungan.
(2) Layanan kesehatan yang komprehensif sebagaimanadimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:
a. upaya promotif, preventif, kuratif dan rehabilitatif untukpelayanan kesehatan dasar;
b. pembebasan dari beban biaya bagi anak gizi buruk, anakpenyandang disabilitas, anak berkebutuhan khusus, anakyang terinfeksi HIV/ AIDS, pekerja anak, anakkorbanpenyalahgunaan narkotika, alkohol, psikotropikadanzat adiktif lainnya, anak yang menjadi korbankekerasan,dan anak korban perdagangan orang;
(3) Pemerintah Daerah, masyarakat, keluarga danorangtuawajib mengusahakan agar Anak yang lahir terhindar dari penyakit yang mengancam kelangsungan hidupdan/ataumenimbulkan kecacatan.

translated_text:
Article 59
(1) Regional Governments are obligated to provide comprehensive health services for Children, so that every Child obtains optimal health status from the time in the womb.
(2) Comprehensive health services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative efforts for basic health services;
b. exemption from cost burden for malnourished children, children with disabilities, children with special needs, children infected with HIV/AIDS, child workers, children who are victims of narcotics abuse, alcohol, psychotropic substances and other addictive substances, children who become victims of violence, and children who are victims of human trafficking;
(3) Regional Governments, communities, families and parents are obligated to endeavor to ensure that Children who are born are protected from diseases that threaten survival and/or cause disability.

text:
Pasal 60
(1) Upaya promotif pelayanan kesehatan dasar sebagaimanadimaksud dalam Pasal 59 ayat (2) huruf a ditujukanuntukmeningkatkan derajat kesehatan secara lebih optimal.
(2) Upaya promotif sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan memberikan sosialisasi ataupenyuluhankepada masyarakat mengenai pola hidup sehat yangmeliputi:
a. pentingnya air susu ibu ekslusif bagi bayi;
b. pentingnya imunisasi bagi balita;
c. pola hidup bersih;
d. pentingnya makanan bergizi; dan e. bahaya narkoba dan merokok.
(3) Selain upaya promotif sebagaimana dimaksud padaayat (2),Pemerintah Daerah dapat melakukan kegiatanlaindalamrangka penyeleggaraan kesehatan.

translated_text:
Article 60
(1) Promotive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 59 paragraph (2) letter a are aimed at improving health status in a more optimal manner.
(2) Promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by providing socialization or education to the community regarding healthy lifestyle patterns which include:
a. the importance of exclusive breast milk for infants;
b. the importance of immunization for toddlers;
c. clean living patterns;
d. the importance of nutritious food; and
e. the dangers of narcotics and smoking.
(3) In addition to promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (2), the Regional Government may carry out other activities in the context of the implementation of health.

text:
Pasal 61
(1) Upaya preventif pelayanan kesehatan dasar sebagaimanadimaksud dalam Pasal 59 ayat (2) huruf a ditujukanuntukmencegah terjadinya penyakit atau permasalahankesehatan.
(2) Upaya sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukandengan:
a. mewajibkan pada ibu untuk pemberian ASI ekslusif padabayi sampai usia 6 (enam) bulan;
b. pemberian imunisasi dan vitamin gratis pada bayi danbalita;
c. pemberian makanan bergizi kepada balita dari keluargakurang mampu;
d. mengoptimalkan peran posyandu untuk pelayanankesehatan bagi ibu dan balita;
e. melakukan pemeriksaan kesehatan secara berkala; f. menyediakan sarana sanitasi dan air bersihdisetiapsekolah; dan
g. menyediakan fasilitas khusus menyusui atauruanganpojok ASI di instansi pemerintah atau dunia usaha.

translated_text:
Article 61
(1) Preventive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 59 paragraph (2) letter a are aimed at preventing the occurrence of disease or health problems.
(2) The efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by:
a. obligating mothers to provide exclusive breastfeeding to infants up to 6 (six) months of age;
b. providing free immunization and vitamins to infants and toddlers;
c. providing nutritious food to toddlers from underprivileged families;
d. optimizing the role of posyandu for health services for mothers and toddlers;
e. conducting periodic health examinations;
f. providing sanitation facilities and clean water at every school; and
g. providing special breastfeeding facilities or breastfeeding corner rooms at government agencies or business entities.

text:
Pasal 69
(1) Kebijakan pengembangan KLA diarahkan pada pemenuhanhak Anak yang terbagi dalam 5 (lima) kelompok, meliputi : a. hak sipil dan kebebasan;
b. lingkungan keluarga dan pengasuhan alternatif; c. kesehatan dasar dan kesejahteraan;
d. pendidikan, pemanfaatan waktu luang, dankegiatanbudaya; dan
e. perlindungan khusus.
(2) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai kebijakan pengembanganKLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diatur denganPeraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 69
(1) The policy for the development of KLA is directed towards the fulfillment of Children's rights which are divided into 5 (five) groups, comprising:
 a. civil rights and freedoms;
 b. family environment and alternative care;
 c. basic health and welfare;
 d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and
 e. special protection.
(2) Further provisions regarding the policy for the development of KLA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Regent's Regulation.

text:
Pasal 70
(1) Dalam rangka efektifitas pelaksanaan kebijakanKLAdi Daerah dibentuk Gugus Tugas KLA.
(2) Gugus Tugas KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),mempunyai tugas pokok:
a. mengkoordinasikan pelaksanaan kebijakandanpengembangan KLA;
b. melakukan sosialisasi, advokasi dan komunikasi informasi dan edukasi kebijakan KLA;
c. mengumpulkan data dasar pengembangan KLA; d. melakukan analisis kebutuhan yang bersumber dari datadasar;
e. melakukan deseminasi data dasar;
f. menentukan fokus dan prioritas programdalammewujudkan KLA, yang disesuaikan denganpotensi daerah;
g. menyusun rencana aksi daerah Kota Layak Anak5(lima) tahunan dan mekanisme kerja; dan h. melakukan monitoring, evaluasi dan pelaporanpalingsedikit 1 (satu) tahun sekali.
(3) Pembentukan Gugus Tugas KLA sebagaimana dimaksudpadaayat (1) ditetapkan dengan Keputusan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 70
(1) In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of the KLA policy in the Region, a KLA Task Force is established.
(2) The KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), has the following main duties:
 a. coordinating the implementation of policies and development of KLA;
 b. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on KLA policy;
 c. collecting baseline data for KLA development;
 d. conducting needs analysis based on baseline data;
 e. conducting dissemination of baseline data;
 f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing KLA, which are adjusted to regional potential;
 g. preparing a 5 (five) year KLA (Child-Friendly City) regional action plan and work mechanism; and
 h. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least 1 (one) time per year.
(3) The establishment of the KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

